# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit .env.local — see .gitignore.
# Required by code-standards.md §12 ("`.env.example` lists every variable with a dummy value")
# and §22 (full table with secret classification).
#
# ⚠️ Two tiers, and the difference matters:
#
#   VALIDATED TODAY (lib/env.ts) — app refuses to boot if missing or malformed:
#     APP_DEFAULT_LOCALE · APP_SUPPORTED_LOCALES · NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY · SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#   VALIDATED WHEN PRESENT (D38) — SUPABASE_DB_POOL_URL: optional until the first
#     direct Postgres consumer exists; a wrong shape is still refused.
#
#   DOCUMENTED, NOT YET VALIDATED — their features are not built. Requiring a PSP
#   key before the PSP adapter exists would block boot for a feature nobody can
#   call. Each feature ADDS ITS KEYS to lib/env.ts as it lands (15 PSP,
#   25 notifications). Until then a missing value here fails at first
#   use, not at startup — so treat this list as a TODO, not a guarantee.
#
#   REQUIRED ON A DEPLOYMENT (lib/deployment.ts, spec 0004, D71) — a Vercel build
#   or any production build or `next start` refuses to run without them, naming
#   each one. A LOCAL `npm run build` or `npm start` therefore sets APP_LOCAL_ONLY=1
#   (the e2e wrapper and the CI build already do). `npm run dev` needs none of it.
#
# ── The one rule about NEXT_PUBLIC_ ──────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ ships the value to every browser. There is no legitimate reason
# for a service role key, a PSP key, or a messaging key to carry that prefix.
# The guard hook blocks it; this file must not model it.

# ─── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public — safe in the browser. RLS is what protects the data, not this key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ_dummy_anon_key

# SECRET — bypasses RLS entirely. Webhooks and cron only, never a user request.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ_dummy_service_role_key

# SECRET — transaction-mode POOLER url (port 6543), not the direct connection.
# Direct connections are for migrations only; serverless will exhaust Postgres.
# Prepared statements must be disabled on this connection. See architecture.md §33.
SUPABASE_DB_POOL_URL=postgresql://postgres.ref:pw@aws-0-region.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true

# ─── Supabase MCP server (.mcp.json) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Read-only MCP access for schema and policy inspection during development.
# The supabase MCP server stays disconnected until both are set — that is expected,
# not a fault. Playwright and Context7 MCP need no credentials at all.
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=your-project-ref
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_dummy_personal_access_token

# Context7 MCP — version-accurate library docs. Runs anonymously without this;
# a key only raises the rate limit. Get one at context7.com, then add an
# Authorization: Bearer header to the context7 entry in .mcp.json.
CONTEXT7_API_KEY=

# ─── PSP adapters — credentials PER REGION ───────────────────────────────────
# One deployment serves both regions, so several PSPs can be configured at once.
# At launch (2026-11-28, D65) only Turkey is live (D22): iyzico Marketplace (D23).
# The adapter is chosen from `regions.psp_provider` for the row being processed —
# never from an env var. Build against the PaymentProvider interface; never
# import a PSP SDK outside lib/psp/. Sandbox keys in dev and staging, never live.

# Turkey — iyzico Marketplace (Pazaryeri)
IYZICO_BASE_URL=https://sandbox-api.iyzipay.com
IYZICO_API_KEY=dummy_iyzico_api_key
IYZICO_SECRET_KEY=dummy_iyzico_secret_key
# SECRET — verifies webhook signatures against the RAW body. The webhook is the
# only proof of payment; a browser redirect never is. See code-standards.md §8.
IYZICO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=dummy_iyzico_webhook_secret

# Saudi Arabia — DEFERRED (D22). PayTabs was the earlier assumption; the Saudi
# PSP is chosen before the KSA launch (Q7). mada support is mandatory.
PAYTABS_BASE_URL=https://secure.paytabs.sa
PAYTABS_PROFILE_ID=dummy_paytabs_profile_id
PAYTABS_SERVER_KEY=dummy_paytabs_server_key
PAYTABS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=dummy_paytabs_webhook_secret

# ─── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Swappable channel so Phase 1 is not blocked by the undecided market.
OTP_CHANNEL=phone
SMS_API_KEY=dummy_sms_api_key

# ─── Notifications ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Queued through the outbox, never sent inline in a request path.
EMAIL_API_KEY=dummy_email_api_key
WHATSAPP_API_KEY=dummy_whatsapp_api_key

# ─── App config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ There is NO global APP_REGION or APP_CURRENCY (D14). Both regions run from
# one deployment, and region is a COLUMN read from the owning row — the request,
# the provider. Currency comes from `regions.currency` for that row.
# A global region constant here would be read as truth and silently mis-scope
# every query the moment the second market goes live.
APP_DEFAULT_LOCALE=ar
APP_SUPPORTED_LOCALES=ar,tr,en

# Marks a local production build or `next start`, never a deployment. Exactly 1,
# or unset; any other value is refused at boot. NEVER set it on Vercel: the build
# and the boot both refuse that pair, because it would switch the key checks off.
# APP_LOCAL_ONLY=1

# ─── Money kill switches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not environment variables (D70). The five flags (funding, unlock, payouts,
# auto release, notifications) are platform_settings rows per region, read live
# on every call by lib/flags and failing closed: flipping a row in the Supabase
# table editor takes effect on the next read, with no deploy.

# ⛔ Stays OFF until written legal sign-off is recorded in progress-tracker.md.
# A stored, pre-loadable balance is what makes a platform a money transmitter.
FEATURE_STORED_BALANCE_WALLET=false
